{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3044d8e0829b9033c758033e1648098b154eea21e3fee1a48508f3c9f3592065"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"General review mode uses /github_webhook_general and /gitlab_webhook_general endpoints, producing one Markdown summary comment per changed file."},{"claim_ids":["clm_396e42fa69bc837f1a30d9234051ea7a4a9f83ba4a702fdb5ac1fc5a20972ac4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Global configuration is loaded from environment variables; runtime changes made via the admin panel take effect immediately but are reloaded from environment variables on restart, so env vars are recommended for persistent global config."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6138bea51456dccdd3e0db49e591a3621735e944f7a9ca3fa801c056b6caace6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: local development involves cloning the repo, creating a virtualenv, installing requirements.txt, starting via python -m api.ai_code_review_helper, and optionally running tests with python -m unittest discover tests."},{"claim_ids":["clm_68018abaa9014456143de0f2fff6cad64915eb4d9f678bd3697f56be506d768d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A web admin panel at /admin and a RESTful config API under /config/* manage webhook secrets, tokens, LLM parameters, and notification URLs; API calls require an X-Admin-API-Key header."},{"claim_ids":["clm_77a60106b50a8efcf8930d54d6c1044dbc5ed8dae3ac1fe253d9c87f22823919"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Detailed review mode exposes endpoints /github_webhook and /gitlab_webhook, where the AI analyzes each changed file and the system converts JSON model output into multiple structured comments."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8cbd85d3da138c27986b2cee0f3b2b16d04f20e37eb37b63e29c21ec6d76dbf6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product is described as an LLM-based automated code review assistant that listens to PR/MR changes via GitHub/GitLab webhooks, analyzes code with AI, and posts review comments automatically."},{"claim_ids":["clm_90d14d723cedaa225fa03f89f1a71b2ea300a22381b6ca7a81e49949f3837a5b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Review summaries including PR/MR links, branch info, and result overviews can be sent to WeCom (enterprise WeChat) bots and custom webhook URLs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a033501be3f935dcac4603724d8dd5cad1bcb8df43119dac84db8cdc79cf62d7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Redis stores repository/project configuration, processed commit SHAs, and AI review results with a default 7-day expiry; records for closed/merged PRs/MRs are cleaned up, and the service strongly depends on Redis."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cbff012f3a7b26bf9641db0e59fabdfc3190c788db2c395a756ce8bbee7960a4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The service posts review comments asynchronously, publishes a summary comment after all files are reviewed, and uses Redis to prevent duplicate reviews of the same commit."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ce1fa3b20b7cc33e0e8c5d38e4d76cd84a5d5e9dd570e746367f5eaa2041c6fe"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration uses OpenAI-compatible LLM settings (OPENAI_API_KEY, OPENAI_MODEL defaulting to gpt-4o, and an optional OPENAI_API_BASE_URL)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d2f8e3791403402fcbcaba41b263f0cd625cf38438b5dd1c956aad14f498420e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"All admin operations are authenticated with a key set via the ADMIN_API_KEY environment variable, whose default value is documented and flagged as must-change."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3044d8e0829b9033c758033e1648098b154eea21e3fee1a48508f3c9f3592065","clm_396e42fa69bc837f1a30d9234051ea7a4a9f83ba4a702fdb5ac1fc5a20972ac4","clm_6138bea51456dccdd3e0db49e591a3621735e944f7a9ca3fa801c056b6caace6","clm_68018abaa9014456143de0f2fff6cad64915eb4d9f678bd3697f56be506d768d","clm_77a60106b50a8efcf8930d54d6c1044dbc5ed8dae3ac1fe253d9c87f22823919","clm_8cbd85d3da138c27986b2cee0f3b2b16d04f20e37eb37b63e29c21ec6d76dbf6","clm_90d14d723cedaa225fa03f89f1a71b2ea300a22381b6ca7a81e49949f3837a5b","clm_a033501be3f935dcac4603724d8dd5cad1bcb8df43119dac84db8cdc79cf62d7","clm_cbff012f3a7b26bf9641db0e59fabdfc3190c788db2c395a756ce8bbee7960a4","clm_ce1fa3b20b7cc33e0e8c5d38e4d76cd84a5d5e9dd570e746367f5eaa2041c6fe","clm_d2f8e3791403402fcbcaba41b263f0cd625cf38438b5dd1c956aad14f498420e"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:28:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_9cff3bd119624badacf9a7467aca74be","id":"pg_0cf712b6da58582f9b5f49815722a58d","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/usagi-org-ai-code-review-helper-readme-md-d5fe002184e9-49815722a58d.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_b2718afb11f55f5ebf6a124f1e05e591"],"title":"Usagi-org/ai-code-review-helper/README.md @ d5fe002184e9","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:28:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9cff3bd119624badacf9a7467aca74be"}
